$$
 L:=\left\lfloor m^{1-1/k}/\ell^2\right\rfloor < R(P).
\tag{3}
$$
*For every $0<\eta<1/2$ a reversible quantum algorithm with $O_k(1+\log(1/\eta))$ queries on every input computes $P$ with error at most $\eta$ on its domain. There is an exact fan-in-two circuit with $S=O_k(m\ell^2)$ gates whose two outputs are the domain bit of $P$ and, on the domain, its value.*", "status": "unverified"}
